<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<RSLogix5000Content SchemaRevision="1.0" SoftwareRevision="16.03" TargetType="AddOnInstructionDefinition" ContainsContext="true" Owner="Dale Reed, Rockwell Automation" ExportDate="Fri Jul 31 10:31:27 2009" ExportOptions="References Context">
<Controller Use="Context" Name="ProcessObjix">
<DataTypes Use="Context">
</DataTypes>
<AddOnInstructionDefinitions Use="Context">
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Use="Target" Name="L_ABS" Revision="1.0" RevisionExtension="00 Release" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="false" CreatedDate="2009-06-23T14:20:15.609Z" CreatedBy="Not Available" EditedDate="2009-07-31T14:31:12.220Z"
 EditedBy="Not Available" SoftwareRevision="v16.03">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Absolute Value (64-bit)]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[Initial Release]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[This instruction returns the absolute value (positive magnitude) of an input
64-bit integer (LINT) value.]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
<Parameters>
<Parameter Name="Inp" DataType="LINT" Usage="InOut" Radix="Decimal" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Input]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Out" DataType="LINT" Usage="InOut" Radix="Decimal" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Output = | Input |]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
</Parameters>
<LocalTags>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Out" DataType="DINT" Dimensions="2" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[32-bit portions of Output]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Inp" DataType="DINT" Dimensions="2" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[32-bit portions of Input]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_LoOvflw" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Low-order 32-bit overflow (without minor fault)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_HiOvflw" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[High-order 32-bit overflow (without minor fault)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Output the absolute value (positive magnitude) of the input]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
L_ABS : 64-bit Absolute Value ( Output = |Input| )
============================================================
Revision 1.0-00 Release:  2009-Jun-31
Initial Release
============================================================
Returns the absolute value (positive magnitude) of the input 64-bit integer (LINT) value.

This instruction breaks the LINT input into two DINTs
(32-bit signed each) to do the math.
===================================================
CONVERT LINT TO DINTs
===================================================
This COPy takes the input LINT and breaks it into a pair of DINTs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Inp,Wrk_Inp[0],2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[===================================================
IF THE INPUT IS NEGATIVE, NEGATE THE VALUE
===================================================
To do a 2's complement (negate) a number, complement it
(invert all the bits), then add 1.

The first branch complements (NOTs) all the bits.
The remaining branches do the increment.
We could just add 1 and do a carry, but we would generate
math Minor Faults on an overflow (from 16#7fff_ffff to 16#8000_0000).
So we check for this special value and handle it in a way that won't
cause a minor fault.  If there's a carry in the (unsigned) add of the
low-order bits, add it to the high-order bits (again, in a way that
does not generate a minor fault).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Inp[1].31)[NOT(Wrk_Inp[0],Wrk_Out[0]) NOT(Wrk_Inp[1],Wrk_Out[1]) ,EQU(Wrk_Out[0],16#7FFF_FFFF) MOV(16#8000_0000,Wrk_Out[0]) OTE(Wrk_LoOvflw) ,XIO(Wrk_LoOvflw) ADD(Wrk_Out[0],1,Wrk_Out[0]) ,EQU(Wrk_Out[0],0) [EQU(Wrk_Out[1],16#7FFF_FFFF) MOV(16#8000_0000,Wrk_Out[1]) OTE(Wrk_HiOvflw) ,XIO(Wrk_HiOvflw) ADD(Wrk_Out[1],1,Wrk_Out[1]) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[===================================================
CONVERT DINTs TO LINT
===================================================
If the Input is negative, the first branch's COPy takes the output pair of DINTs
from the Negate above and combines them into a single output LINT (64-bit signed integer).

If the Input is positive, the second branch's COPy just copies the Input to the Output.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_Inp[1].31) COP(Wrk_Out[0],Out,1) ,XIO(Wrk_Inp[1].31) COP(Inp,Out,1) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
